So I did it , my first ascension. For moments it seemed impossible but
I did it. Sure I'm about as spoiled as can be but still I did it :)

Mandatory longwinded report.

Pissemedkatt's journey started out as a protection run. Collected gold
& items through the first five levels and then straight to Minetown.
Turns out minetown had no general store, so all the items was for
nothing. Didn't really feel like cloning money since it feels rather
abusive. Got two points of protection. But with dwarven mithril,
dwarven helmet, iron boots and shield AC was below -2 anyway

While there were no general store in Minetown, there were however one
on level 5, so I went there to sell the goods instead and make another
trip to get more protection. Accidentally stumbled into and kills a
shrieker and gains a level (not the first kill in the game though).
Then and there gave up any ideas for immediate protection. As a final
nail in the coffin my pet cat diappears and I'm stuck all alone in the
mines. Priest was non-aligned btw.

Went to sokoban, and on my way there got Excalibur; and collected an
amulet of reflection, one I wore for the most part  of the game. Found
a bag some levels later which I first mistook for a normal sack, but
it turns out to be a bag of holding. Returned down the mines and got
the lucksone, got the candles and continued down the main branch
again.

Found two aligned Priests, though none were lawful. The first one was
nice place to stash stuff and donate money. Went deeper in pursuit of
stuff.

Stumbled into a silver dragon, which left me her scales. Used my
first ?oEnchant armor. Annoyingly I had so far found about 4-6 scrolls
of enchant armor, but no armor worth enchanting. Got the silverscales
to +4 and life seemed much more ... feasible. Please note that I made
a huge, massive, enourmos mistake here. I misread silver for gray.
Since I already had reflection and now was convinced I had magic
resistance the path continued downward. AC ~ 14-18

Got to medusas level, but only with a potion of levitation to get me
over to her place, no instrument and no letters of charming I had no
way to bring the dragon to the altar (pun intended).

Returned back up the branch in search of more stuff. Thought I might
do the quest, but no ring or boots of levitation would make that very
dangerous. Two wraiths got me to lvl 14, and I thought what the hell.
There could be a pair of levvy boots there? I promise I'll be very
careful not to step in the lava, pretty please?
It turned out to be all right. Lord surtur got struck by a potion of
Paralysis and was mowed down by our heroine.

Interrestingly, I had so far  found several potions of healing and
extra healing. Considered alchemizing them now that the numbers was
worth it, and thus went for an altar. On the  intended altar level
suddeny a black pudding stirs. Never having tried the pudding farming
technique myself I thought, why not try it, eh?. But there was the
priest thingie guarding the altar jealously. He must be convieniently
removed from office, and since i had reflection and magic
resistance(!!), he can't be that bad.

Actually he wasn't , but he could've been. Donned the robe and
enchanted it to +4. Then a orcish dulled dagger started to divide the
puddings, and the result was twofold. My god decided I should have
every possible artifact available to lawful characters and that there
were slightly too many puddings available. I actually got so many
artifacts that I wondered which I should use. Decided that Grayswandir
and a silversabre would do as a primary weapon. Kept the sunsword,
excalibur and frostbrand in my BOH as backup weapons.
 Noteworthy as well was that I got a magic lamp from the loot, though
it was never used as anything but as a light sourcet. Also, a pair of
speedboots could be recovered from the loot. Most other stuff was
stashed, and never used again.

Now it was time to alchemize, and some potions needed to be diluted
first. On my way to the water I found a pair of boots of levitation.

10 blessed diluted potions of healing later, medusa turned to stone by
her own gaze. Persepheus got to keep his scimitar.

The castle was a piece of cake, went in the back door and took out the
four dragons first. Realizing only when the dragons were dead that I
was satiated and couldn't have a snack of the black dragon, sigh. The
wand resulted in scroll of charging, a pair of gauntlets of power
and , finally having realized my mistake,  a cloak of magic
resistance. Donned my new equipment, only to find another pair of
gauntlets of power in the castle-storage. Next time, search first,
wish later.

Fireproofed my armor and enchanted the cloak and went down into the
valley. Nothing special really. Continued down into Gehennom, paid off
Asmodeus and Bhaalzebub and killed Juiblex. Went back up to get some
more protection.  AC ~ 22-25.

Had almost no holy water with me, but decided it wasn't time to get
more right now, but rather to map the dungeon get back up dilute/bless
water and back down. Found Vlad more by mistake than on purpose. Also
found 7 candles scattered in Gehennom. Very handy since my candle
stash was in Sokoban :). The vibrating square was in the middle of lvl
48. Engraved some squares around it and dropped the bell and
candelabrum.

Got struck by an mindflayer and, in a very cowardly move,  decided I
should backtrack the whole dungeon to make sure I knew the way.
Tedious, but quickly done. At the moment I was at level 25 with 380 HP
and AC -35, weilding +7 Grayswandir and a +6 silver sabre. Wrested a
wish from my wand of wishing and got a ring of conflict.

Went for Rodney and got the book. Rushed to the square and (for the
first time every) invoked the items.
The high priest of Moloch had invited Rodney for a cup of tea,  twice!
Two zaps with a wand of death made sure the tea-party was over. In the
same square, there were now three amulets of yendor. Found out which
the real one was and ran for it. The mysterious force apparently
decided I should stay in Juiblex swamp, as I passed it five times. But
other than that the acension run was simple.

Plane of earth was cake, same with air. Fire was annoying, all the 15
turns I spend there. Water slightly confusing, but I accidentally
stumbled into the portar wearing the ring of conflict.

The Astralplane wasn't at all what I had imagined. Definitely not as
open as I've always thought, and definitely more crowded. Decided I
didn't want to know whether the riders could open doors and went to
the right first. Killed pestilence, twice, and found out that the
altar was neutral. Went back, had a unwanted mele=E9 with Death and to
my joy found out that the altar was Lawful. With no hesitation offered
the amulet to Tyr and ascended.

Finally.

Remarks: Found a single wand of teleportation in the whole game, and
that one had zero charges.

Thank you all you people here on rgrn!

